  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REDUCING THE ILLEGAL TRADE IN SOFTSHELL TURTLES IN WEST BENGAL - INDIA, USING AN INTERDISCIPLINARY APPROACH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO REDUCE THE ILLEGAL SALE AND TRAFFICKING OF MEAT FROM SEVERAL SPECIES OF ENDANGERED SOFTSHELL TURTLES INCLUDING THE NARROW-HEADED SOFTSHELL TURTLE, INDIA SOFTSHELL TURTLE AND PEACOCK SOFTSHELL TURTLE WITHIN A HOTSPOT HOSTING SOME OF THE LARGEST MEAT MARKETS ALONG THE INDO-BANGLADESH BORDER. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) CONDUCTING INTERVIEWS WITH INFORMANTS AND STAKEHOLDERS AND SYNTHESIZING AND ANALYZING THESE DATA, ALONG WITH TEN YEARS OF SEIZURE DATA, TO INFORM THE DEVELOPMENT OF DEMAND REDUCTION ACTIVITIES, AND 2) IMPLEMENTING DEMAND REDUCTION ACTIVITIES, LIKE BEHAVIOR CHANGE CAMPAIGNS.</narrative>
  </description>
